# Git workflow rules

## Protected branches

- **Never** commit or push directly to `dev`, `staging`, or `main`.
- All work lands via PR from task branches.

## Branch naming

- Tasks: `feature/[sprint]/[task-id]-[slug]`
- Example: `feature/S001/T004-add-checkout-step`

## Pull requests

- **PR description is mandatory** — use the template from `skills/close/SKILL.md`.
- Task PRs target **`dev`** only.
- Milestone PRs target **`staging`** from `dev` (human merges).

## After merge

- Delete the feature branch locally and on remote after merge.
- Keep `dev` updated before starting a new task branch.

## Factory system branches

```
main          ← you merge staging → main manually
staging       ← milestone PRs (you approve)
dev           ← task PRs (agents)
feature/...   ← one branch per task
```

## Commits on feature branches

- Conventional Commits; small logical commits allowed.
- No merge commits from protected branches into feature branches without reason.

## Do not

- Force-push `dev`, `staging`, or `main` without explicit user request
- Squash history on shared branches without project policy
